 {"id": "DF-0925-07", "title": "P1 Multi-host DR pull cannot restore a fresh machine: `s3 sync <ns> pull` errors 'Namespace not found' on an empty namespaces root, `sync all pull` succeeds restoring 0 namespaces (silent), and pulled JSONL arrives without git history — the README's 'pull on another machine = DR + shared memory' needs an undocumented `namespace create` first and delivers data-only", "priority": "P1", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "created_by": "dogfood", "complexity": 2, "detail": "Dogfood run 11 (2026-09-25, S3-tier angle; real bucket duckbrain, scratch prefix duckbrain-dogfood-s3, isolated via DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH/CONFIG_PATH + scratch auth). Verified working: manifest autopush of a written namespace (6 objects incl. manifest.json + _audit/current.jsonl within ~30s of commit debounce), delta push byte-exact (file sizes local==remote), SQL over S3 via DuckDB httpfs (count + projections, 3.6-3.9s incl. DuckDB boot), pull->boot daemon->9/9 memories read back, write-after-restore (201) + explicit push (uploaded=2 skipped=4) + pull on root A (downloaded=2) -> running daemon on root A saw root B's 11 writes with NO restart. The DR promise fails exactly at fresh-machine restore: (1) `s3 sync dfs3-journal pull` into an empty namespaces root -> 'Error: Namespace not found: dfs3-journal' (pull resolves the namespace from the LOCAL config, src/s3/sync.ts); (2) `s3 sync all pull` -> '[S3] pull complete: 0 namespaces, 0 files transferred' exit 0 — silent success while restoring NOTHING (a user believes their DR restore worked); (3) after undocumented `duckbrain namespace create dfs3-journal` the pull works (6 files, 4.6s) but the namespace git repo stays EMPTY ('master' has no commits) — git history never travels through this path and nothing on the S3 side carries it. ACCEPTANCE: (a) pull materializes namespaces found under the remote prefix (bootstrap-then-pull) or a documented bootstrap flag exists; (b) 'all pull' reports restored-vs-skipped loudly and never claims success with 0 restored when the prefix is non-empty; (c) README/docs show the exact fresh-machine restore command sequence that a user can paste on an empty root and get a serving daemon."}
 {"id": "DF-0925-08", "title": "P2 S3 surface gaps: no documented path wires the s3daily git-mirror remote for a NEW namespace (autopush git history never fires); README's 'global git identity required' is false on a fresh box; `s3 status` lists only config-registered namespaces so a live S3-backed namespace is invisible on its own surface", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "created_by": "dogfood", "complexity": 2, "detail": "Same run. (1) README's Native S3 flow (enable s3.enabled -> s3 status -> s3 sync all push -> s3 query) never mentions `git remote add s3daily s3://duckbrain/current/git/<ns>`; the AUTOPUSH-001 hook (selectPushRemote, src/git/autocommit.ts) does nothing for a namespace with no remotes — proven live: scratch ns repo had zero remotes, the 30s debounce committed, the s3.enabled manifest/JSONL autopush DID fire, but no git bundles ever landed; docs/s3-native.md documents the push mechanism in depth but not the one-time setup step, and getting-started's 'S3 storage tier needs git-remote-s3 + AWS CLI' says nothing about per-namespace remotes. (2) Fresh-host extras claim a global git identity is REQUIRED for the git-backed store: an ephemeral fresh Ubuntu 24.04 agent with NO git identity passed the full README verify sequence (namespace create/write/read-back all fine, daemon stamped the synthetic 'duckbrain@localhost.localdomain' author — corroborates GIT-IDENTITY-001); the README claim is stale. (3) `s3 status` enumerates config namespaceMappings only (src/s3/cli.ts): an API-created namespace that exists, accepts writes, and is actively pushed to S3 does not appear in the per-ns sync listing (same registry split-brain as DF-0924-06, observed from the S3 surface). ACCEPTANCE: (a) one documented command to wire a namespace for S3 (remote add + verify) referenced from README + docs/s3-native.md + skills/duckbrain-usage; (b) README fresh-host extras corrected to match reality; (c) s3 status enumerates the on-disk namespaces root unioned with config registrations (reuses the DB-GAP-057 union-list fix)."}
