 {"id": "DF-0926-02", "title": "P1 GET /api/memories silently ignores undocumented ?key= and ?query= params — the repo's own http-api example teaches both, and each returns 200 with the UNFILTERED list instead of filtering or 400", "priority": "P1", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-26", "created_by": "dogfood", "complexity": 2, "detail": "Run 12 discriminator proof: 2 memories written (keys /examples/http/test content 'Hello from HTTP API!...', /examples/http/second content 'Uniquely different zebra content'). GET /api/memories?key=%2Fexamples%2Fhttp%2Ftest → BOTH items; GET /api/memories?query=zebra → BOTH items. Neither param exists in docs/api/http-api.md's query table (prefix/domain/author/q/contains/after/before/between/as_of/attr/historical/limit/offset/namespace); the server accepts unknown params without error. A client following examples/http-api/client.js believes it queried one key / one search and gets everything — silent wrong results, worse than a 400. Documented routes verified working: /api/memories/key/:key (single-key read-back exact id), ?contains=, ?q= (keyword fallback 200 without a provider). ACCEPTANCE: (a) unknown query params are rejected 400 listing valid params (or at minimum ?key/?query alias to real behavior); (b) examples/http-api/client.js recall()/search() use documented params."}
 {"id": "DF-0926-03", "title": "P1 ?contains= keyword search deterministically misses terms present verbatim in stored content (Hello/from/different → 0 hits; zebra/API/content hit) — stable across search-index rebuild (rowCount 2) and the 30s commit debounce", "priority": "P1", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-26", "created_by": "dogfood", "complexity": 2, "detail": "Run 12: 2-row namespace on scratch daemon :3821. contains=Hello → total 0 (both casings) though the row content is 'Hello from HTTP API! @ ...' and 'Hello' greps in the namespace JSONL AND in .search/fts.duckdb-adjacent files. contains=zebra → 1 (correct), Zebra → 1 (case-insensitive where it works), API → 1, content → 1, examples → 2; from → 0, different → 0, HTTP → 2. Misses survived the documented escape hatch: `duckbrain search-index rebuild` reported default rowCount 2 / durationMs 237, re-probe unchanged; also unchanged after the git auto-commit debounce fired (2 commits). Pattern is per-term deterministic, not staleness — the index writer drops or mis-tokenizes some terms while the query half works. Keyword search is the documented offline fallback for ?q= (503 EMBEDDINGS_UNAVAILABLE path), so a missing term is a silent false negative for agents. ACCEPTANCE: (a) repro test: write contents 'Hello from HTTP API' + 'zebra', rebuild, assert contains=Hello AND contains=zebra both hit; (b) failing terms above used as regression fixtures."}
